    <cmt>Te Araroa</cmt>
    <desc>4ème plus long chemin de randonnée au monde, s'étendant de Cape Reinga à Bluff
---
Te Araroa is New Zealand's long distance tramping route, stretching circa 3,000 kilometres along the length of the country's two main islands from Cape Reinga to Bluff. Officially opened in 2011, it is made up of a mixture of previously made tracks and walkways, new tracks, and link sections alongside roads. Tramping the full length of the trail generally takes three to six months.
[[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Te_Araroa|Wikipedia]]
